ecial needs",\n            "Focusing primarily on accommodations for physical disabilities",\n            "Using Universal Design for Learning principles",\n            "Emphasizing the same expectations for all children"\n          ],\n          correctAnswer: 2,\n          explanation: "Universal Design for Learning (UDL) involves creating environments and experiences that work for all children by offering multiple means of engagement, representation, and action/expression.",\n          domain: "Inclusive Practices",\n          points: 10\n        },\n        {\n          question: "Which statement best describes executive function skills in young children?",\n          options: [\n            "Skills that develop naturally without adult intervention",\n            "Skills primarily focused on academic achievement",\n            "Working memory, inhibitory control, and cognitive flexibility",\n            "Skills that only develop after age five"\n          ],\n          correctAnswer: 2,\n          explanation: "Executive function skills include working memory, inhibitory control (self-regulation), and cognitive flexibility, which are crucial for learning and development.",\n          domain: "Cognitive Development",\n          points: 10\n        }\n      ],\n      level3: [\n        {\n          question: "In the context of the Reggio Emilia approach, what is meant by the \'hundred languages of children\'?",\n          options: [\n            "Children should learn multiple spoken languages",\n            "Children express themselves through many symbolic languages beyond speech",\n            "Curriculum should include exactly one hundred learning activities",\n            "Teachers should provide explicit instruction in many subject areas"\n          ],\n          correctAnswer: 1,\n          explanation: "The \'hundred languages\' refers to the many ways children express, explore, and understand, including drawing, movement, sculpture, dramatic play, and other symbolic representations.",\n          domain: "Educational Approaches",\n          points: 15\n        },\n        {\n          question: "According to Vygotsky\'s sociocultural theory, what role do adults play in children\'s development?",\n          options: [\n            "They should allow children to develop naturally with minimal intervention",\n            "They facilitate learning through scaffolding within the Zone of Proximal Development",\n            "They directly teach skills through repetition and reinforcement",\n            "They primarily serve as evaluators of developmental progress"\n          ],\n          correctAnswer: 1,\n          explanation: "Vygotsky emphasized that learning occurs through social interactions, with adults scaffolding within the Zone of Proximal Development (the gap between what a child can do independently and what they can do with support).",\n          domain: "Developmental Theory",\n          points: 15\n        },\n        {\n          question: "Which approach to early childhood assessment most effectively captures authentic learning?",\n          options: [\n            "Standardized testing administered at regular intervals",\n            "Documentation of children\'s work and teacher observations over time",\n            "Weekly quizzes on academic content",\n            "Comparison of children\'s abilities against normative benchmarks"\n          ],\n          correctAnswer: 1,\n          explanation: "Documentation of children\'s work, conversations, and teacher observations over time provides authentic assessment of learning in context, rather than isolated test performance.",\n          domain: "Assessment",\n          points: 15\n        },\n        {\n          question: "When implementing trauma-informed care in early childhood settings, which approach is most effective?",\n          options: [\n            "Maintaining strict routines with consequences for all behavioral issues",\n            "Focusing primarily on academics to help children overcome trauma",\n            "Creating predictable environments with emotional support and regulation strategies",\n            "Avoiding topics that might trigger trauma responses"\n          ],\n          correctAnswer: 2,\n          explanation: "Trauma-informed care includes creating predictable, safe environments, building relationships, teaching emotional regulation strategies, and understanding behaviors as communication of needs.",\n          domain: "Social-Emotional Development",\n          points: 15\n        }\n      ]\n    };\n\n    // DOM Elements\n    const progressFill = document.getElementById(\'progress-fill\');\n    const questionCounter = document.getElementById(\'question-counter\');\n    const pointsCounter = document.getElementById(\'points-counter\');\n    const questionText = document.getElementById(\'question-text\');\n    const optionsContainer = document.getElementById(\'options-container\');\n    const feedbackElement = document.getElementById(\'feedback\');\n    const submitBtn = document.getElementById(\'submit-btn\');\n    const nextBtn = document.getElementById(\'next-btn\');\n    const levelInfo = document.getElementById(\'level-info\');\n    \n    // Results elements\n    const quizSection = document.getElementById(\'quiz-section\');\n    const resultsSection = document.getElementById(\'results-section\');\n    const finalScore = document.getElementById(\'final-score\');\n    const finalFeedback = document.getElementById(\'final-feedback\');\n    const domainAnalysis = document.getElementById(\'domain-analysis\');\n    const restartBtn = document.getElementById(\'restart-btn\');\n\n    // Quiz state\n    let currentQuestion = 0;\n    let totalQuestions = 10;\n    let currentLevel = 1;\n    let points = 0;\n    let selectedOption = null;\n    let questions = [];\n    let correctInARow = 0;\n    let incorrectInARow = 0;\n    let domainScores = {};\n\n    // Initialize quiz\n    function initQuiz() {\n      // Reset state\n      currentQuestion = 0;\n      points = 0;\n      currentLevel = 1;\n      correctInARow = 0;\n      incorrectInARow = 0;\n      domainScores = {};\n      \n      // Generate questions\n      generateQuestions();\n      \n      // Show quiz, hide results\n      quizSection.style.display = \'block\';\n      resultsSection.style.display = \'none\';\n      \n      // Load first question\n      loadQuestion();\n      updateProgress();\n    }\n\n    // Generate questions for the quiz\n    function generateQuestions() {\n      questions = [];\n      \n      // Start with level 1 questions\n      const level1Qs = [...questionsData.level1];\n      const level2Qs = [...questionsData.level2];\n      const level3Qs = [...questionsData.level3];\n      \n      // Shuffle all question arrays\n      shuffle(level1Qs);\n      shuffle(level2Qs);\n      shuffle(level3Qs);\n      \n      // Take 4 questions from each level to ensure a good mix\n      questions.push(...level1Qs.slice(0, 4));\n      questions.push(...level2Qs.slice(0, 3));\n      questions.push(...level3Qs.slice(0, 3));\n      \n      // Shuffle final question set to randomize order\n      shuffle(questions);\n      \n      // Set total questions\n      totalQuestions = questions.length;\n    }\n\n    // Shuffle array (Fisher-Yates algorithm)\n    function shuffle(array) {\n      for (let i = array.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {\n        const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));\n        [array[i], array[j]] = [array[j], array[i]];\n      }\n      return array;\n    }\n\n    // Load current question\n    function loadQuestion() {\n      const question = questions[currentQuestion];\n      \n      // Update level display based on points value\n      if (question.points === 5) {\n        currentLevel = 1;\n        levelInfo.textContent = "Level 1 - Foundational Knowledge (5 points per question)";\n        levelInfo.style.backgroundColor = \'#f0f9ff\';\n        levelInfo.style.borderColor = \'#bae6fd\';\n        levelInfo.style.color = \'#0369a1\';\n      } else if (question.points === 10) {\n        currentLevel = 2;\n        levelInfo.textContent = "Level 2 - Intermediate Knowledge (10 points per question)";\n        levelInfo.style.backgroundColor = \'#f0f7ff\';\n        levelInfo.style.borderColor = \'#93c5fd\';\n        levelInfo.style.color = \'#1e40af\';\n      } else {\n        currentLevel = 3;\n        levelInfo.textContent = "Level 3 - Advanced Knowledge (15 points per question)";\n        levelInfo.style.backgroundColor = \'#f5f3ff\';\n        levelInfo.style.borderColor = \'#c4b5fd\';\n        levelInfo.style.color = \'#5b21b6\';\n      }\n      \n      // Set question text\n      questionText.textContent = question.question;\n      \n      // Clear options container\n      optionsContainer.innerHTML = \'\';\n      \n      // Add options\n      question.options.forEach((option, index) => {\n        const optionElement = document.createElement(\'div\');\n        optionElement.classList.add(\'option\');\n        optionElement.textContent = option;\n        optionElement.dataset.index = index;\n        \n        optionElement.addEventListener(\'click\', () => {\n          selectOption(index);\n        });\n        \n        optionsContainer.appendChild(optionElement);\n      });\n      \n      // Reset state for new question\n      selectedOption = null;\n      submitBtn.disabled = true;\n      submitBtn.style.display = \'block\';\n      nextBtn.style.display = \'none\';\n      feedbackElement.style.display = \'none\';\n      \n      // Update question counter\n      questionCounter.textContent = `Question ${currentQuestion + 1} of ${totalQuestions}`;\n    }\n\n    // Select an option\n    function selectOption(index) {\n      selectedOption = index;\n      \n      // Update UI\n      const options = document.querySelectorAll(\'.option\');\n      options.forEach(option => {\n        option.classList.remove(\'selected\');\n      });\n      \n      options[index].classList.add(\'selected\');\n      submitBtn.disabled = false;\n    }\n\n    // Submit answer\n    function submitAnswer() {\n      const question = questions[currentQuestion];\n      const isCorrect = selectedOption === question.correctAnswer;\n      \n      // Track domain performance\n      if (!domainScores[question.domain]) {\n        domainScores[question.domain] = {\n          correct: 0,\n          total: 0,\n          points: 0\n        };\n      }\n      \n      domainScores[question.domain].total++;\n      \n      if (isCorrect) {\n        points += question.points;\n        domainScores[question.domain].correct++;\n        domainScores[question.domain].points += question.points;\n        correctInARow++;\n        incorrectInARow = 0;\n        \n        // Show points animation\n        showPointsAnimation(question.points);\n      } else {\n        incorrectInARow++;\n        correctInARow = 0;\n      }\n      \n      // Update UI\n      const options = document.querySelectorAll(\'.option\');\n      \n      if (isCorrect) {\n        options[selectedOption].classList.add(\'correct\');\n        feedbackElement.classList.add(\'correct\');\n        feedbackElement.classList.remove(\'incorrect\');\n        feedbackElement.innerHTML = `\n          <strong>Correct!</strong> ${question.explanation}\n          <p>You earned ${question.points} points!</p>\n        `;\n      } else {\n        options[selectedOption].classList.add(\'incorrect\');\n        options[question.correctAnswer].classList.add(\'correct\');\n        feedbackElement.classList.add(\'incorrect\');\n        feedbackElement.classList.remove(\'correct\');\n        feedbackElement.innerHTML = `\n          <strong>Incorrect.</strong> The correct answer is: ${question.options[question.correctAnswer]}\n          <p>${question.explanation}</p>\n        `;\n      }\n      \n      feedbackElement.style.display = \'block\';\n      submitBtn.style.display = \'none\';\n      nextBtn.style.display = \'block\';\n      \n      // Update points display\n      pointsCounter.textContent = `${points} points`;\n    }\n\n    // Show points animation\n    function showPointsAnimation(pointValue) {\n      const animation = document.createElement(\'div\');\n      animation.classList.add(\'points-animation\');\n      animation.textContent = `+${pointValue}`;\n      \n      // Position near the question\n      const rect = questionText.getBoundingClientRect();\n      animation.style.left = `${rect.right - 50}px`;\n      animation.style.top = `${rect.top}px`;\n      \n      document.body.appendChild(animation);\n      \n      // Remove after animation completes\n      setTimeout(() => {\n        document.body.removeChild(animation);\n      }, 1500);\n    }\n\n    // Move to next question\n    function nextQuestion() {\n      currentQuestion++;\n      \n      // Adjust difficulty based on performance\n      if (currentQuestion < totalQuestions) {\n        // Adaptive difficulty - modify upcoming questions if possible\n        if (correctInARow >= 2 && currentQuestion + 1 < totalQuestions) {\n          // Try to increase difficulty of next question\n          for (let i = currentQuestion + 1; i < totalQuestions; i++) {\n            if (questions[i].points < 15) {\n              let nextLevel;\n              \n              if (questions[i].points === 5) nextLevel = \'level2\';\n              else nextLevel = \'level3\';\n              \n              // Find a replacement question from higher level\n              const possibleReplacements = questionsData[nextLevel].filter(q => \n                !questions.some(existingQ => existingQ.question === q.question)\n              );\n              \n              if (possibleReplacements.length > 0) {\n                // Replace with a higher difficulty question\n                const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * possibleReplacements.length);\n                questions[i] = possibleReplacements[randomIndex];\n                break;\n              }\n            }\n          }\n          \n          correctInARow = 0;\n        } else if (incorrectInARow >= 2 && currentQuestion + 1 < totalQuestions) {\n          // Try to decrease difficulty of next question\n          for (let i = currentQuestion + 1; i < totalQuestions; i++) {\n            if (questions[i].points > 5) {\n              let nextLevel;\n              \n              if (questions[i].points === 15) nextLevel = \'level2\';\n              else nextLevel = \'level1\';\n              \n              // Find a replacement question from lower level\n              const possibleReplacements = questionsData[nextLevel].filter(q => \n                !questions.some(existingQ => existingQ.question === q.question)\n              );\n              \n              if (possibleReplacements.length > 0) {\n                // Replace with a lower difficulty question\n                const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * possibleReplacements.length);\n                questions[i] = possibleReplacements[randomIndex];\n                break;\n              }\n            }\n          }\n          \n          incorrectInARow = 0;\n        }\n        \n        loadQuestion();\n        updateProgress();\n      } else {\n        showResults();\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Update progress bar\n    function updateProgress() {\n      const progress = ((currentQuestion) / totalQuestions) * 100;\n      progressFill.style.width = `${progress}%`;\n    }\n\n    // Show quiz results\n    function showResults() {\n      quizSection.style.display = \'none\';\n      resultsSection.style.display = \'block\';\n      \n      // Set final score\n      finalScore.textContent = points;\n      \n      // Calculate accuracy\n      let totalCorrect = 0;\n      let totalQuestionsTaken = 0;\n      \n      Object.values(domainScores).forEach(domain => {\n        totalCorrect += domain.correct;\n        totalQuestionsTaken += domain.total;\n      });\n      \n      const accuracy = totalCorrect / totalQuestionsTaken * 100;\n      \n      // Generate feedback based on score\n      let feedback;\n      if (points >= 100) {\n        feedback = `Excellent work! You scored ${points} points with ${accuracy.toFixed(0)}% accuracy. You have a strong understanding of early childhood education principles.`;\n      } else if (points >= 70) {\n        feedback = `Good job! You scored ${points} points with ${accuracy.toFixed(0)}% accuracy. You have a solid foundation in early childhood education with some areas to strengthen.`;\n      } else {\n        feedback = `You\'ve taken an important first step and scored ${points} points with ${accuracy.toFixed(0)}% accuracy. Keep exploring these concepts to build your knowledge.`;\n      }\n      \n      finalFeedback.textContent = feedback;\n      \n      // Generate domain analysis\n      domainAnalysis.innerHTML = \'<h3>Domain Analysis</h3>\';\n      \n      // Sort domains by performance (percentage correct)\n      const sortedDomains = Object.entries(domainScores)\n        .map(([domain, stats]) => ({ \n          domain, \n          percentage: (stats.correct / stats.total) * 100,\n          points: stats.points,\n          correct: stats.correct,\n          total: stats.total\n        }))\n        .sort((a, b) => b.percentage - a.percentage);\n      \n      // Display strengths\n      const strengthsDiv = document.createElement(\'div\');\n      strengthsDiv.innerHTML = \'<h4 style="color: #059669;">Strengths</h4>\';\n      \n      const strengths = sortedDomains.filter(d => d.percentage >= 70);\n      if (strengths.length > 0) {\n        const strengthsList = document.createElement(\'ul\');\n        strengths.forEach(domain => {\n          const li = document.createElement(\'li\');\n          li.textContent = `${domain.domain}: ${domain.correct}/${domain.total} correct (${domain.percentage.toFixed(0)}%)`;\n          strengthsList.appendChild(li);\n        });\n        strengthsDiv.appendChild(strengthsList);\n      } else {\n        strengthsDiv.innerHTML += \'<p>Keep practicing to develop your strengths.</p>\';\n      }\n      \n      // Display growth areas\n      const growthDiv = document.createElement(\'div\');\n      growthDiv.innerHTML = \'<h4 style="color: #d97706;">Growth Areas</h4>\';\n      \n      const growthAreas = sortedDomains.filter(d => d.percentage < 70);\n      if (growthAreas.length > 0) {\n        const growthList = document.createElement(\'ul\');\n        growthAreas.forEach(domain => {\n          const li = document.createElement(\'li\');\n          li.textContent = `${domain.domain}: ${domain.correct}/${domain.total} correct (${domain.percentage.toFixed(0)}%)`;\n          growthList.appendChild(li);\n        });\n        growthDiv.appendChild(growthList);\n      } else {\n        growthDiv.innerHTML += \'<p>Great job! You did well across all domains.</p>\';\n      }\n      \n      domainAnalysis.appendChild(strengthsDiv);\n      domainAnalysis.appendChild(growthDiv);\n    }\n\n    // Event listeners\n    submitBtn.addEventListener(\'click\', submitAnswer);\n    nextBtn.addEventListener(\'click\', nextQuestion);\n    restartBtn.addEventListener(\'click\', initQuiz);\n\n    // Start the quiz\n    initQuiz();\n  </script>\n', PosixPath('public/standalone-ece-quiz.html'), 'config..semgrep.vendored-rules.html.security.audit.insecure-document-method') match_id = 6a9f988459f3ffbda603b5de946d6b11ce8edb5a2fe9d17152ddacb0b7609d7823f017e44b93e50a7e717d404cc12911c6ec39a5ad3f14750429aab0eb340343_0
